2. Models and pretrained components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The benchmark compares LeWM, PLDM and DINO-WM using the training schemes
specified in the technical report. Project-trained checkpoints and upstream
pretrained components are distinguished there. Model weights are not included
in the dataset package and are not covered by its generated-data license.
Upstream pretrained components retain their original terms and attribution.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Stable-WorldModel — evaluation runtime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

    https://github.com/galilai-group/stable-worldmodel
    License: MIT

Provides the world-model implementations and simulator backends that the
benchmark's adapters load. Installed as a separate dependency; NOT REDISTRIBUTED in the data package.
The training and evaluation records identify the runtime revision used for
each reported result.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Environments
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The nine capability tasks are constructed on four environments — TwoRoom,
PushT, Reacher and Cube — reached through Stable-WorldModel. PushT, the
DeepMind Control Reacher task and the OGBench Cube task originate with their
respective upstream projects and remain under their own licenses. ContextWorld
contributes the hidden-dynamics factor variation, the paired context/query
construction, and the evaluation protocol layered on top of them; those
contributions are the material covered by DATA_LICENSE.


